Description: gnome-free icon pack for the VibeOS launcher
 gnome-free (called Round before VibeOS): colourful icons for VibeOS's apps
 and the GNOME apps it keeps, a white Material Symbols glyph on a gradient
 disc in each app's colour. VibeOS Settings' Home screen switches packs.

Package: vibeos-iconpack-vibeos
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: vibeos-launcher,
Description: VibeOS icon pack for the VibeOS launcher
 The VibeOS icons, the launcher's default: a large Material Symbols glyph on
 a squircle in each app's colour (white on colour, or coloured on white), for
 VibeOS's apps and the GNOME apps it keeps. Installing it makes it the
 launcher's icon pack; VibeOS Settings' Home screen switches packs.

Package: vibeos-parallax-solar-system
Architecture: all
Conflicts: neo-parallax-solar-system
Replaces: neo-parallax-solar-system
Provides: neo-parallax-solar-system
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: vibeos-launcher,
Description: NASA solar-system parallax wallpaper for the VibeOS launcher
 A layered wallpaper that moves with the device's tilt on the VibeOS
 launcher: the Sun, Earth, the Moon, Mars, Saturn and Jupiter from NASA's
 public-domain images over a drawn star field. Installing it makes it the
 default wallpaper; GNOME Settings' Background panel lists it too.

